 "title": "Webster County Assessor",
 "text": "Webster County Assessor\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nHome\nCounty\nAbout\nEmployment\nHistory\nHistorical Information\nVisitors Committee Grant App\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor's\nOffice\nGIS Workshop\nSales Files\nAttorney\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nClerk\nClerk's Office\nBirth Certificate Info\nMarriage License\nMilitary\nDischarge\nProperty Valuation\nProtests\nSpecial\nLicenses\nCounty Court\nClerk of the District Court\nDistrict\nCourt Office\nCourt Filing Fees\nSelf Help\nElection Commissioner\nElection Commissioner's\nOffice\nElection Information\nLocal Election Results\nEmergency Manager\nExtension\nOffice\nHighway Department\nPlanning and Zoning\nRegister of\nDeeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nTreasurer's\nOffice\nBoating Guide\nBoating Registration\nDriver's\nExam\nDrivers Licenses\nTitles and Registration\nUnclaimed Property\nVeterans Services Officer\nWeed Superintendent\nCalendar\nContacts\nOffice Links\nOffice Services\nOther Organizations\nFeedback\n-->\nAssessor\nPhone\n402-746-2717\nFax\n402-746-2715\nAddress\n621 N Cedar St\nRed Cloud, NE 68970\nLinks\nCertification of Valuation\nProperty Taxes Explained\nHow Property Assessment\nand Taxation Works\n1987-1988 to Present Budget Request Information\n2023-2024 Levy Overview\n2022-2023 Levy Pie Charts\nNameplace Capacity Tax\n2011 to Current\nAssessor Sales File\nAssessor Appraisal Information\nNebraska Department of Property\nAssessment and Taxation\nNebraska Tax Equalization\nand\nReview Commission\nState Surveyors Office\nHomestead\nExemption Information Nebraska Department of Revenue\nPersonal Property\nReal Estate\nHomestead Exemptions\nGeneral FAQ's\nPermissive Exemptions FAQ's\nMobile Homes FAQ's\nProtest Instructions - This form must be attached to your\nprotest.\nEditable Property Valuation Protest, Form 422A\nTami\nScheuneman\n|\nAssessor\n|\nCarla Jameson\n|\nDeputy Assesor\n|\nLeigh Goebel\n|\nClerk\n|\nElizabeth Sitzman\n|\nClerk\n|\nPart-time Clerk Position Available\nJob Description\nApplication\n-->\nThe County Assessor is an elected official who\nhas general supervision over and the direction of the assessment of\nall property in Webster County for taxation purposes. Their\nprimary duty is to uniformly and proportionately value all real\nproperty (land, homes and buildings) within the county.\nQualifications\nMust hold a current Assessor’s Certificate\nMust obtain 60 hours of continuing education every 4 year\nterm\nDuties\nPrimary duty is to uniformly and proportionately establish\nand maintain market value on all real property in the county\nusing mass appraisal.\nResponsible for maintaining personal property accounts on\nall business’ and farmers who own depreciable personal property.\nMaintain parcel maps; GIS and Cadastral\nAttend all meetings of County Board of Equalization\nReview all applications for Permissive Exemptions such as\nreligious, charitable and educational.\nAdminister the Homestead Exemption Program\nPrepare numerous State reports\nCertify values to political subdivisions\nPrepare annual tax roll for county Treasurer\nMaintain accounts on all State Assessed property\nValuation changes are due to changes in the\nmarket, the addition or removal of improvements, remodel or\nrehabilitation of the property or deterioration of the property.\nIt is not our job to raise your value to get more tax dollars it is\nour job to establish and maintain uniform and proportionate values\non all real property within the county. We then take it to the\npercentage set by State Statute for that class of property.\nThe Assessor does not levy or collect taxes. How much your\ntaxes are will be determined by each political subdivisions budget.\nThe levies are set by the County Commissioners using the budget\nagainst the value of each political subdivision.\nAll information, except the actual Homestead\nExemption Application is public record. You can obtain any\ninformation we have on file about any property in the County; such\nas size of lot, size and age of home or value of property.\nCopyright © 2012 MIPS Inc. All rights reserved. |\nDisclaimer\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
